@model WorkshopModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Overview"; }
<p class="eyebrow">ASP.NET CORE + SQLITE</p><h1>Feature management.<br />Inside your own app.</h1>
<p class="lead">Change a feature in the packaged dashboard, then refresh this workshop to see your application take a different path. Everything runs locally.</p>
<section class="card"><h2>Your first toggle</h2><ol><li><a href="/internal/features">Open the embedded dashboard</a> and initialize the empty catalog.</li><li>Create a feature with key <code>new-dashboard</code>. New features start disabled.</li><li>Visit <a href="/gates">Declarative gates</a>: the classic fallback appears.</li><li>Enable the feature in the dashboard, then refresh the gates page. The new dashboard branch replaces it.</li></ol><p>For the complete workshop, upload <code>example-catalog.json</code> on <a href="/internal/features/import">Import</a>, review its preview, and apply the additions. If you already created a key, explicitly choose whether to replace it.</p></section>
<h2>Live flag checklist</h2><p>Keys are stable identifiers used in code; names and descriptions are editable labels. These are real SDK evaluations for <strong>@Model.Persona.Name</strong> and <strong>@Model.Persona.Order.Id</strong>.</p>
<div class="flag-grid">@foreach (var key in FeatureFlags.Demo) { <article class="card flag"><code>@key</code><strong class="@(Model.Flags[key] ? "on" : "off")">@(Model.Flags[key] ? "ON" : "OFF")</strong></article> }</div>
<section class="card"><h2>Explore the application boundaries</h2><p><a href="/gates">Razor gates</a> remove disabled markup. <a href="/programmatic">Programmatic checks</a> select a server behavior. <a href="/identity">Request identity</a> and <a href="/orders">Order context</a> answer “for whom?” and “for which entity?”. Compare the <a href="/filters">filters matrix</a>, then learn about <a href="/integrations">persistence and cloud migration</a>.</p><p>This workshop demonstrates Boolean features. Embedded v1 has no variants or experiments; an ON result is not an experiment assignment.</p></section>
